+What if you're not using @command{gawk}?  You can write a separate
+@code{BEGIN} rule that loops over the files named in @code{ARGV}
+and attempts to read a record with @code{getline}.  If @code{getline}
+immediately returns zero (end of file), the file exists but is empty.
+You can then delete it from @code{ARGV}, issue a warning, or do
+anything else you think is appropriate.
+
+Also, we note that this library routine was written when @command{gawk}
+(like its maintainer) was considerably younger.  In modern versions,
+you could instead write it like this:
+
+@example
+ENDFILE @{
+    if (FNR == 0)
+            zerofile(FILENAME, ARGIND)
+@}
+@end example
