+@cindex @env{AWKLIBPATH} environment variable, on MS-Windows
+Similarly, the @env{AWKLIBPATH} environment variable, which tells
+@command{gawk} where to look for dynamic extensions (@pxref{Dynamic
+Extensions}), also uses semicolons to separate directories.  If not
+set in the environment, the default value hard-coded into
+@command{gawk} is @samp{@w{d:/usr/lib/gawk/ext-@var{api-version}}},
